## 13. Integrating with Hyprland

The window opens borderless (no decorations) and transparent, 900×640 by
default (min 480×360) — it is meant to be launched/floated by your compositor.

Example bindings in `hyprland.conf`:

```ini
# Launch / focus HyprTodo
bind = $mainMod, T, exec, hyprtodo

# Float it like a launcher-style overlay
windowrulev2 = float, class:^(hyprtodo)$
windowrulev2 = size 900 640, class:^(hyprtodo)$
```

Because there are no window decorations, close HyprTodo with your usual WM
kill binding (`$mainMod, Q` → `killactive` by default) — there is currently no
in-app quit shortcut.

---

## 14. Current limitations

Be aware of what is **not implemented yet**:

- No Hyprland IPC yet (no workspace-aware tasks, no show/hide toggle).
- Task editing, search, filtering, sorting, undo: not available. Criticality,
  due dates, descriptions, and subtasks are data-model-ready and CLI/GUI-API
  reachable, but have no GUI controls.
- No D-Bus notifications/reminders.
- Theme and keybindings are hardcoded (dark GitHub-ish palette); Lua can only
  configure categories and columns today.
- Deleting/completing actions are instant and irreversible (no undo stack).
- The Waybar module reports pending count only; no critical/overdue badge yet.
- Mouse interaction is essentially unused by design.

